  "configuration_id": "config_039",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best configuration (config_038: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, concat) achieves 0.721 accuracy, clearly outperforming the RNA-only best (0.653) and the resnet50 multimodal (0.688). This confirms that scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + multiprofile is the strongest design combination. However, all multimodal experiments so far have used concat fusion; weighted fusion has never been tested. Question: config_039 changes only the fusion method (concat → weighted) while holding every other design choice identical to config_038, cleanly isolating the effect of fusion strategy. Why this is the best next experiment: It is a single-variable, high-information experiment that directly tests whether a more expressive fusion mechanism can further improve on the current best. If weighted fusion helps, we gain a concrete performance improvement; if it does not, we confirm concat is sufficient and can redirect budget toward other unexplored axes (e.g., image-only ablation or scgpt in multimodal). Under a limited budget, exploiting the strongest known direction with a minimal, well-isolated change is more efficient than a broader exploratory jump."
}

